@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] changelog-copies-pully-format
Settings' changelog and the once-after-update notice MUST use the same Pully
bottom sheet titled What's new, with a fixed centered header and floating cross,
shared drag/detent/Back behavior and a scrolling body. Each version is an unboxed
block: small muted version, New badge on the newest, optional bold summary, plain
group headings and accent-dot bullets with 12dp spacing. Versions are separated
by a hairline, 24dp top padding and 28dp bottom padding. Bundled illustrations
appear under their associated bullet, rounded and framed, at most 420dp tall.
The sheet uses the app's font like every other screen. This layout MUST NOT
change update permission, install, download or once-after-install bookkeeping.
Source: Tavi, 22 October 2026: "literally copy exactly the format from Pully for
the changelog. It's a bottom sheet." pulls.review UpdateUi.kt WhatsNewSheet,
