@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] update-screen-is-required
When the server offers a newer release, Inventory MUST show only the update screen, over
everything, from the first frame of a start: "Inventory 0.6.72 is ready", "Update to keep
using Inventory.", every newer version with its notes, and "Update to 0.6.72" as the main
action. Nothing MUST close it but the update, and Back MUST leave the app. The phone
remembers the last offer, so a start shows the screen before the server answers again;
a failed check keeps the offer and a server with nothing newer takes it away. Updates
MUST NOT start installing by themselves when the user leaves the app; an update the user
started carries on (update-carries-on-when-you-leave). Source: Tavi, 5 Nov 2026
("updating when you open and not letting you use until updated. Like Pully"); pulls.review
update-screen-is-required and updater-remembers-the-offer. The app's name changed from
ThyMind to Inventory on Tavi's word, 5 Nov 2026 ("fully rename it to Inventory everywhere").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] update-shows-its-progress
Update MUST download (when the package is not on the phone yet), wait for any upload in
flight and install in the app, showing how far it got in place. Without Android's
install permission, Update MUST open its settings page and carry on by itself when the
user comes back allowing it. A failed download or install MUST offer Try again, and an
approval Android still waits for MUST offer Continue update; neither lets the user
through. Source: Tavi, 5 Nov 2026; pulls.review update-shows-its-progress and
update-confirmation-remains-actionable.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] update-notifies-once
While the app is closed, the background check MUST download a newer release and tell the
user in a notification once per version; its tap opens the app on the update screen.
Source: Tavi, 5 Nov 2026; pulls.review updater-notifies-once.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] update-carries-on-when-you-leave
Once the user taps Update (or Try again), the download, the wait for uploads in flight and
the hand-off to Android MUST carry on when the user leaves the app, with an ongoing
notification that shows the download's percent, the wait for an upload and the install;
its tap opens the update screen. When Android then needs the user's tap, a notification
MUST ask for it; when the update stops while the user is away (a failed download or
install, not a cancel of Android's prompt), a notification MUST say so and its tap opens
the update screen with Try again. Source: Tavi, 7 Nov 2026 ("once we start an update in
the app, we gotta make sure it happens even if you leave the app as it downloads or
installs!"). The wording of the notifications is Claude's choice, not confirmed by Tavi.
